---

<a class='skip-link' href='#main-content'>Skip to content</a>

<header class='site-header'>
  <nav class='nav-shell' aria-label='Primary navigation'>
    <a class='brand' href='/' aria-label='Anhao Li home'>Anhao Li</a>
    <div class='nav-links'>
      <a href='#about'>About</a>
      <a href='#news'>News</a>
      <a href='#research'>Research</a>
      <a href='#publications'>Publications</a>
      <a href='#experience'>Experience</a>
      <a href='#awards'>Awards</a>
      <a class='cv-link' href='/cv.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>CV</a>
      <a class='blog-link' href='/blog'>Blog</a>
      <button
        class='theme-toggle'
        id='personal-theme-toggle'
        type='button'
        aria-label='Toggle color theme'
      >
        <span aria-hidden='true'>◐</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </nav>
</header>

<main id='main-content'>
  <section class='hero' aria-labelledby='hero-title'>
    <div class='hero-shell'>
      <div class='hero-text'>
        <p class='eyebrow'>AI Agents · Large Language Models</p>
        <h1 id='hero-title'>Anhao Li</h1>
        <p class='hero-role'>
          Computer Science Undergraduate ·
          <a href='https://twin-cities.umn.edu/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
            University of Minnesota Twin Cities
          </a>
        </p>
        <p class='lead'>
          I work on AI agents and large language models, with a focus on long-horizon terminal tasks
          — the kind that take hundreds of steps, where the hard part is not a single answer but
          staying on course.
        </p>
        <p class='hero-note'>
          Most of what I build sits between systems and evaluation: agent infrastructure that runs
          reliably, and benchmarks that show whether an agent actually made progress. Outside
          research, I compete in ICPC and coach competitive programming.
        </p>
        <div class='hero-actions'>
          <a class='action primary' href={`mailto:${email}`}>
            <Icon name='email' />
            <span>Email me</span>
          </a>
          <a class='action' href='/cv.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
            <Icon name='document' />
            <span>CV</span>
          </a>
          <a class='action' href={scholarUrl} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
            <SimpleIcon name='googlescholar' size='15' />
            <span>Scholar</span>
          </a>
          <a class='action' href={githubUrl} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
            <Icon name='github' />
            <span>GitHub</span>
          </a>
          <a class='action' href={linkedinUrl} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
            <span class='linkedin-mark' aria-hidden='true'>in</span>
            <span>LinkedIn</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class='hero-photo'>
        <Image
          src={portrait}
          alt='Portrait of Anhao Li'
          class='portrait'
          width={620}
          height={784}
          densities={[1, 1.5]}
          loading='eager'
        />
      </figure>
    </div>

    <dl class='highlight-strip'>
      {
        highlights.map((item) => (
          <div class='highlight'>
            <dt>{item.value}</dt>
            <dd>{item.label}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>

  <div class='page-shell'>
    <section class='section' id='about'>
      <div class='section-rail'>
        <h2>About</h2>
      </div>
      <div class='section-body prose-block'>
        <p>
          I am an undergraduate in Computer Science at the University of Minnesota Twin Cities. My
          research centers on AI agents and large language models — specifically, how an agent can
          sustain progress across a task that unfolds over hundreds of terminal steps, and how we
          can tell, from the outside, whether it is actually getting anywhere.
        </p>
        <p>
          That question pulls in two directions, and I work in both. On the systems side, I build
          agent infrastructure and evaluation harnesses — the plumbing that lets long runs execute
          reproducibly. On the measurement side, I work on benchmarks and grading methods that
          reward partial progress instead of collapsing a long trajectory into a single pass/fail
          bit. This has led to two recent preprints, and to two summers of engineering work on LLM
          agent infrastructure and data tooling at VecML.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before research, competitive programming shaped how I think about problems. I have
          competed for about ten years — NOI and USACO in China, then ICPC in the United States —
          and in 2026 our team became the first from Minnesota in a decade to reach the ICPC World
          Finals. I now coach the university team, and I still find that the habits from contest
          practice carry over: decompose the problem, bound the cost, verify before you commit.
        </p>
        <p class='currently'>
          <span>Currently</span> preparing for the ICPC World Finals and coaching the UMN team, while
          continuing research on agent evaluation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='section' id='news'>
      <div class='section-rail'>
        <h2>News</h2>
        <p class='rail-note'>Recent updates</p>
      </div>
      <div class='section-body'>
        <div class='news-list'>
          {
            news.map((item) => (
              <article class='news-item'>
                <p class='mono-meta'>{item.date}</p>
                <div class='news-content'>
                  <p class='tag'>{item.category}</p>
                  <h3>
                    <a
                      href={item.href}
                      target={item.href.startsWith('http') ? '_blank' : undefined}
                      rel={item.href.startsWith('http') ? 'noreferrer' : undefined}
                    >
                      {item.title}
                      <span class='arrow' aria-hidden='true'>
                        {item.href.startsWith('http') ? '↗' : '→'}
                      </span>
                    </a>
                  </h3>
                  <p class='muted'>{item.description}</p>
                </div>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='section' id='research'>
      <div class='section-rail'>
        <h2>Research Interests</h2>
        <p class='rail-note'>What I spend my time on</p>
      </div>
      <div class='section-body'>
        <div class='research-grid'>
          {
            researchInterests.map((interest) => (
              <article class='research-card'>
                <span class='mono-meta'>{interest.number}</span>
                <h3>{interest.title}</h3>
                <p class='muted'>{interest.description}</p>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='section' id='publications'>
      <div class='section-rail'>
        <h2>Publications</h2>
        <a class='rail-link' href={scholarUrl} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
          All on Scholar ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='section-body'>
        <div class='publication-list'>
          {
            publications.map((publication) => (
              <article class='publication-item'>
                <a
                  class='publication-visual'
                  href={publication.website}
                  target='_blank'
                  rel='noreferrer'
                  aria-label={`Visit the project site for ${publication.title}`}
                >
                  <Image
                    src={publication.image}
                    alt={publication.imageAlt}
                    class='publication-image'
                    loading='lazy'
                  />
                </a>
                <div class='publication-content'>
                  <p class='mono-meta'>
                    {publication.venue} · {publication.year}
                  </p>
                  <h3>
                    <a href={publication.href} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
                      {publication.title}
                    </a>
                  </h3>
                  <p class='authors'>
                    {publication.authors.map((author, index) => (
                      <>
                        {author === 'Anhao Li' ? <strong>{author}</strong> : author}
                        {index < publication.authors.length - 1 ? ', ' : ''}
                      </>
                    ))}
                  </p>
                  <p class='muted publication-summary'>{publication.summary}</p>
                  <div class='publication-meta'>
                    <a href={publication.href} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
                      Paper ↗
                    </a>
                    <a href={publication.website} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
                      Project site ↗
                    </a>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='section' id='experience'>
      <div class='section-rail'>
        <h2>Experience</h2>
      </div>
      <div class='section-body'>
        <div class='row-list'>
          {
            experiences.map((experience) => (
              <article class='row-item'>
                <p class='mono-meta'>{experience.period}</p>
                <div>
                  <h3>{experience.role}</h3>
                  <p class='row-focus'>{experience.focus}</p>
                  <p class='muted'>
                    {experience.company} · {experience.location}
                  </p>
                </div>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='section' id='awards'>
      <div class='section-rail'>
        <h2>Honors & Awards</h2>
        <p class='rail-note'>Selected</p>
      </div>
      <div class='section-body'>
        <div class='award-list'>
          {
            awards.map((award) => (
              <article class='award-item'>
                <div>
                  <h3>{award.title}</h3>
                  <p class='muted'>{award.description}</p>
                </div>
                <p class='mono-meta award-period'>{award.period}</p>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='section' id='education'>
      <div class='section-rail'>
        <h2>Education</h2>
      </div>
      <div class='section-body'>
        <div class='education-heading'>
          <h3>University of Minnesota Twin Cities</h3>
          <p class='mono-meta'>Sep 2024 – Present</p>
        </div>
        <div class='detail-list'>
          <div class='detail-row'>
            <p>Degree</p>
            <p>B.S. in Computer Science</p>
          </div>
          <div class='detail-row'>
            <p>GPA</p>
            <p>3.96 / 4.0</p>
          </div>
          <div class='detail-row'>
            <p>Activities</p>
            <p>Competitive Programming · ICPC Contestant · ICPC Coach, 2026–2027</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='section' id='service'>
      <div class='section-rail'>
        <h2>Teaching & Service</h2>
      </div>
      <div class='section-body'>
        <div class='row-list'>
          {
            service.map((item) => (
              <article class='row-item'>
                <p class='mono-meta'>{item.period}</p>
                <div>
                  <h3>{item.role}</h3>
                  <p class='muted'>{item.detail}</p>
                </div>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='section' id='writing'>
      <div class='section-rail'>
        <h2>Writing</h2>
        <a class='rail-link' href='/blog'>All posts →</a>
      </div>
      <div class='section-body'>
        <p class='section-intro muted'>
          Contest write-ups, technical notes, and the occasional reflection. Most posts are written
          in Chinese.
        </p>
        <div class='post-list'>
          {
            recentPosts.map((post) => (
              <a class='post-item' href={`/blog/${post.id}`}>
                <p class='mono-meta'>{postDateFormatter.format(new Date(post.data.publishDate))}</p>
                <div>
                  {post.data.category && (
                    <p class='tag'>{categoryLabels[post.data.category] ?? post.data.category}</p>
                  )}
                  <h3>{post.data.title}</h3>
                  <p class='muted'>{post.data.description}</p>
                </div>
                <span class='arrow' aria-hidden='true'>
                  →
                </span>
              </a>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='contact-card' id='contact' aria-labelledby='contact-title'>
      <div>
        <p class='eyebrow'>Get in touch</p>
        <h2 id='contact-title'>Happy to talk about agents, evaluation, or contest problems.</h2>
        <p class='muted'>Email is the fastest way to reach me.</p>
      </div>
      <div class='contact-links'>
        <a class='action primary' href={`mailto:${email}`}>
          <Icon name='email' />
          <span>{email}</span>
        </a>
        <div class='contact-secondary'>
          <a href={scholarUrl} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>Google Scholar ↗</a>
          <a href={githubUrl} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>GitHub ↗</a>
          <a href={linkedinUrl} target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>LinkedIn ↗</a>
          <a href='/cv.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>CV ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>

<footer class='personal-footer'>
  <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Anhao Li</p>
  <p>Research, code, and notes.</p>
</footer>

<script is:inline type='application/ld+json' set:html={jsonLd} />

<script>
  const themeToggle = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#personal-theme-toggle')
  themeToggle?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const nextTheme = document.documentElement.classList.contains('dark') ? 'light' : 'dark'
    localStorage.setItem('theme', nextTheme)
    document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark', nextTheme === 'dark')
    document
      .querySelector('meta[name="theme-color"]')
      ?.setAttribute('content', nextTheme === 'dark' ? '#131516' : '#f8f8f6')
  })
</script>

<style>
  /* === Shared primitives === */

  .skip-link {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0.75rem;
    left: 0.75rem;
    z-index: 100;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--home-border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--home-surface);
    transform: translateY(-150%);
  }

  .skip-link:focus {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .mono-meta {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--home-muted);
    font-family: 'ComicShannsMono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    line-height: 1.6;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .muted {
    color: var(--home-muted);
  }

  .tag {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    color: var(--home-accent);
    font-size: 0.67rem;
    font-weight: 720;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--home-accent);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 720;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .arrow {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform 160ms ease;
  }

  /* === Header === */

  .site-header {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 20;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--home-border) 82%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--home-background) 90%, transparent);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
  }

  .nav-shell {
    display: flex;
    width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 3rem));
    min-height: 4.25rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .brand {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    font-weight: 720;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .nav-links {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--home-muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  .nav-links a {
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 140ms ease;
  }

  .nav-links a:hover,
  .nav-links a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--home-accent);
  }

  .blog-link {
    padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--home-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--home-foreground) !important;
  }

  .theme-toggle {
    display: grid;
    width: 1.95rem;
    height: 1.95rem;
    padding: 0;
    place-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--home-border);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--home-foreground);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .theme-toggle:hover,
  .theme-toggle:focus-visible,
  .blog-link:hover,
  .blog-link:focus-visible {
